      "scope": "Internal sequential disposable-fixture startup utility; no init function or public preference/concurrency API. Gallery/workbench existing conditional fixture modes only.",
      "existing_spec": "Native-window-lifecycle spec explicitly states no rollback of defaults already applied by a failed load. The proposed nearby function comment makes terminal handling and no in-process retry/ignore visible at the API.",
      "rollback_choice": "Restoring only prior Zoom or saver cannot undo arbitrary Settings.Apply side effects and could falsely imply transactionality. That broader implementation is unnecessary for current terminal startup scope.",
      "test_meaning": "Existing in-memory failure control intentionally permits its Apply to run, yet asserts marker error, nil restore and no installed geometry override. This is compatible with partial loaded defaults; it is not a rollback test."
